That's more or less what I have in mind.

The centerpiece of this engine is a function I call nhvsprintf(), which 
accepts the typestring, the format, and a va_list and returns a malloc'd 
buffer containing the output.  This is the language-independent part, which 
fetches the parameters, interprets the formatters and puts the whole thing 
together.  There's also a language-dependent part, consisting of a 
structure full of function pointers rather like the existing windowing 
interface, which handles all the inflections and such.


